    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d71">

                <pb facs="0182" n="66" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg66"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 893.00/1073.</note>
                <head ana="#head_untitled-inferred-from-preceding-sibling-head">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Peking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-02-16">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 16, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Yuan Shih-Kai unanimously elected President yesterday by the Nanking assembly.
                    To-day the Imperial family and the former Ministers of State all urged him not
                    to decline the office. The provisional capital is fixed at Nanking. Sun
                    telegraphs Yuan that an envoy has been sent to invite him to come to
                    Nanking.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Calhoun.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
